{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הקולות יחדלון והברד לא יהיה עוד", :translit "ha-kolot yechdelun ve-ha-barad lo yihyeh od", :gloss "the voices will cease and the hail will be no more"} {:he "הקולות", :translit "ha-kolot", :gloss "the voices"} {:he "במתן תורה", :translit "be-matan torah", :gloss "at the giving of the Torah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Close reading: Moses says hail 'will be no more' but voices only 'will cease' — a deliberate distinction"}], :frame {:text "At Sinai God descended amid thunder (קולות) and lightning, and the sound of the shofar grew exceedingly strong (Exodus 19:16, Exodus 19:19). Moses himself later recounts that 'the mountain burned with fire up to the heart of heaven, darkness, cloud, and thick darkness' and 'the LORD spoke to you from the midst of the fire, a voice of words you heard' (Deuteronomy 4:11–12). Thus the plague's thunder-voices were only paused, not abolished, because the same voice would reappear to give the Torah.", :sources ["Exodus 19:16" "Exodus 19:19" "Deuteronomy 4:11-12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Close reading: Moses says hail 'will be no more' but voices only 'will cease' — a deliberate distinction", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:14:38.423131416Z", :model "glm-5.2"}